[DEFECT-1] ZERO figures render on any page of this unit.
     imgs=0 and figures=0 on all seven pages in all three views. All eight
     figures (fig-U6-1 .. fig-U6-8) are still Spec 008 `{/* FIGURE[...] */}`
     comment markers at `Status: prompt-only`, and MDX strips comments, so
     nothing reaches the DOM. static/img/figures/efmp-302/unit-06/ does not
     exist. Confirmed visually in
     render/agent-g3-efmp302-u6-run001.topic-01.figure-region.desktop.png:
     under "## A real classroom situation" there is no image, and the next
     paragraph reads "The figure above sets it beside three things ...".
     Six such dangling deictic references were found in the prose
     (topic-01:44, topic-01:111, topic-03:39, topic-03:163, topic-04:44,
     topic-04:92). A learner on the rendered page is pointed at content that
     is not there. `check:figures` passes because a comment marker counts as a
     carrier, which is exactly why this needs a rendered-page check.

[DEFECT-2] ERQ rubric tables are CLIPPED and UNREACHABLE at phone widths.
     Page: /semester-1/efmp-302/unit-06/unit-assessment/ ("### ERQ rubrics").
     At viewport 360px: table box = 328px, but the header row lays out at
     481px wide, right edge x=498.
       "Criterion"     left  17 right 136  visible
       "Limited (1-2)" left 136 right 249  visible
       "Adequate (3)"  left 249 right 376  NOT visible
       "Strong (4-5)"  left 376 right 498  NOT visible
     At viewport 414px the "Strong (4-5)" column is still off-screen (x=376..498).
     There is no recovery path: window.scrollTo(3000,y) leaves scrollX=0,
     html/body overflow-x are both `visible`, and no ancestor of the table has
     overflow-x auto/scroll with scrollWidth > clientWidth. The top performance
     band of all five ERQ rubrics is therefore unreadable on a phone.
     Visual evidence: render/agent-g3-efmp302-u6-run001.unit-assessment.rubric-clip.narrow360.png
                      render/agent-g3-efmp302-u6-run001.unit-assessment.rubric-table.narrow.png
     SCOPE CHECK (diagnostic, at 360px): the same overflow occurs on every
     4-column ERQ rubric table in this course's other assessment pages -
     unit-02 (5 tables, right edges 519-567), unit-05 (5 tables, 475-558),
     unit-06 (5 tables, 492-539). unit-01 has no such table. This is therefore a
     site-wide theme/CSS defect, not something Unit 6 introduced, and it is NOT
     repairable by editing Unit 6 prose. Recorded as an accessibility failure on
